#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae7650e3-faf3-520c-9674-ffa036a8eacc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Power Rule to Compute a Limit"}] :question/id #uuid "9f9e4a39-22c9-5bcf-9b34-b3b1459acb44" :question/math-academy-id "e-30" :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}\\left[(2x-1)^3(x-2)^9\\right].$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we apply the product rule and the power rule to get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}\\left[(2x-1)^3(x-2)^9\\right]   &= \\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}(2x-1)^3\\cdot  \\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}(x-2)^9\\[3pt]\n                                                                                    &= \\left(\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}(2x-1)\\right)^3\\cdot  \\left(\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}(x-2)\\right)^9\\[3pt]\n                                                                                    &= (2\\cdot 3 -1)^3\\cdot (3-2)^9\\[3pt]\n                                                                                    &= 5^3 \\cdot 1^9\\[3pt]\n                                                                                    & = 125.\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054513 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad6d0a4-7854-5f87-896c-0c3ba5ef60af" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Power Rule to Compute a Limit Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "27b89a42-7f31-579b-af21-b33ebe36f749" :question/math-academy-id "e-31" :question/problem "The figure below shows the graph of $f(x).$ Determine $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 2} \\left(\\dfrac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2}\\right)^3.$\n\n![](images/50/5059a2cee34ad8547bf1af6239ab4a8356e715cd920707cf5f33d2de105a5c1d.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we find $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 2} f(x)=3.$ Therefore, using the power rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}{(\\frac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2})}^{3} & ={({lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2-7(2)}{(2\\cdot 3)+2})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-12}{8})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-3}{2})}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{27}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054518 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1bddb74-97be-5f35-b559-afb707e6e964" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Root Rule to Compute a Limit"}] :question/id #uuid "8177157c-4d89-59df-af9b-38f1bee2d6a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-3564" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 1} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{x+8}}{x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{x+8}}{x-2}\n=\\dfrac{\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1} \\sqrt{x+8}}{\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1}(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\nApplying the root rule in the numerator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\sqrt{x+8} & =\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to 1}(x+8)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+8} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the denominator, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}(x-2) & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+8}}{x-2} & =\\frac{3}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "10100e89-21d6-53c5-a7de-f14fd73ce4b7" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Different Rules to Compute a Limit Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "3d6b32ee-3385-5fba-91a5-66c0bbb13dea" :question/math-academy-id "e-3565" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -2}\\left(\\dfrac{f(x)}{x^2-1}\\right)^{2/3}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted below.\n\n![](images/58/583e67513466b35aafcae69c81d5703b45ffada4bdc08bb34de15ee6ce1d53e5.png)" :question/worked-solution "According to the power rule and the quotient rules,\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}{(\\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}-1})}^{2/3} & ={(\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)}{{lim}_{x\\to -2}({x}^{2}-1)})}^{2/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find from the graph that the limit of the numerator is\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -2} f(x)=1.\n$$\n\n We also calculate the limit of the denominator as\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}({x}^{2}-1) & =(-2)^{2}-1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n So we get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}{(\\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}-1})}^{2/3} & ={(\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)}{{lim}_{x\\to -2}({x}^{2}-1)})}^{2/3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2/3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae7650e3-faf3-520c-9674-ffa036a8eacc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Power Rule to Compute a Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0299086f-a9df-5d4c-8a5d-12909499b9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513532} {:answer/id #uuid "0b89a9c1-ae1e-53cd-870b-0b3398dc456d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513559} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea63932-44ee-5257-a860-031d4b22cb5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513566} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2d4ec3-81f9-5c2b-afea-778c89b3e2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513699} {:answer/id #uuid "a47fade5-efa0-5680-99f8-ee4635a935fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b89a9c1-ae1e-53cd-870b-0b3398dc456d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513559} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dc42901-e845-587c-94ce-65c1d0d668eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6909c4f4-167d-501d-93f8-5aca9ebb11ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-100238" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{x\\to -3}\\frac{({x}^{3}-6x+6)^{3}}{(2x+3)^{4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we apply the quotient rule and the power rule to get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -3}\\frac{({x}^{3}-6x+6)^{3}}{(2x+3)^{4}} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to -3}({x}^{3}-6x+6)^{3}}{{lim}_{x\\to -3}(2x+3)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{({lim}_{x\\to -3}({x}^{3}-6x+6))}^{3}}{{({lim}_{x\\to -3}(2x+3))}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{((-3)^{3}-6(-3)+6)^{3}}{(2(-3)+3)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-27+18+6)^{3}}{(-6+3)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)^{3}}{(-3)^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad6d0a4-7854-5f87-896c-0c3ba5ef60af" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Power Rule to Compute a Limit Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0655f199-c8d6-5f17-bcb4-b4b87653a288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513545} {:answer/id #uuid "0713280a-34b2-55f3-8068-2217c2587025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513549} {:answer/id #uuid "22d94631-90ef-5dd0-9744-1800a708cf2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513627} {:answer/id #uuid "3722b946-836c-53bf-b791-729d6bd80951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513679} {:answer/id #uuid "85ebfa28-c0ff-53fb-b392-78cc57c704c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3722b946-836c-53bf-b791-729d6bd80951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513679} :answer-field/id #uuid "99f2c544-09a4-50d1-9061-fcad089e9e54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514299}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbcc700b-75d4-530d-b320-ed65a6308882" :question/math-academy-id "q-100279" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4f8b046dd85d258dd897e595b5dba1116e5df763e2e74a196c6b79e2a8a42a5.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3-x)^{3}(f(x)-4{x}^{2})^{5}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=3.$ \n\nFrom the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3-x)^{3}(f(x)-4{x}^{2})^{5}={lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3-x)^{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(f(x)-4{x}^{2})^{5}.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of each factor, separately.\n\nApplying the power rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3-x)^{3} & ={({lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3-x))}^{3} \\\\  & =(3-1)^{3} \\\\  & ={2}^{3} \\\\  & =8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(f(x)-4{x}^{2})^{4} & ={({lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(f(x)-4{x}^{2}))}^{5} \\\\  & =(3-4(1)^{2})^{5} \\\\  & =(-1)^{5} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3-x)^{3}(f(x)-4{x}^{2})^{5} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(3-x)^{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\,1}(f(x)-4{x}^{2})^{5} \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-8\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514399 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "10100e89-21d6-53c5-a7de-f14fd73ce4b7" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Different Rules to Compute a Limit Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "602172b3-6445-5c63-91e9-d860394ce5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513790} {:answer/id #uuid "71a5e4f2-139f-523f-9c38-312f34b1bd6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513834} {:answer/id #uuid "79827563-1b5d-5c99-902a-4ea904d05b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513851} {:answer/id #uuid "b8839d8b-e0bd-5cb4-8bde-c168499e0d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514020} {:answer/id #uuid "f672a463-52c0-5b34-9a86-4f4728479311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "602172b3-6445-5c63-91e9-d860394ce5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513790} :answer-field/id #uuid "81cfc4b2-47d0-50ed-a06c-623ea25dae23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "522ad648-b326-5d90-9d3d-5351c0a03cfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-100306" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b12ba04b803d58c6cacf4fc781db5c7032c3aedad80506c101bf084109ebd797.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to -2}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4(f(x))^{3}-3{x}^{2}}{2}}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=-1.$\n\nApplying the root rule, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4(f(x))^{3}-3{x}^{2}}{2}} & =\\sqrt[3]{{lim}_{x\\to -2}(\\frac{4(f(x))^{3}-3{x}^{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4\\cdot (-1)^{3}-3(-2)^{2}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{-4-12}{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{-8} \\\\  & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad6d0a4-7854-5f87-896c-0c3ba5ef60af" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Power Rule to Compute a Limit Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c5f42df-3964-5fb9-892c-30fcd5fa6a68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513607} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb21591-e7c1-5eff-a2b9-1c43344e4b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513738} {:answer/id #uuid "4d90c1e2-bb2d-5822-9449-b7e24e15adcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513742} {:answer/id #uuid "ab97757b-cf23-5076-8350-9418e2c28b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513981} {:answer/id #uuid "f748334c-00c1-505b-8c87-f5ee2fe08c12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d90c1e2-bb2d-5822-9449-b7e24e15adcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513742} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ebf540e-bdee-5a9e-a1c5-b91a0a393a38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "948c861d-0397-5eab-9d25-bae477da16f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-17280" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5e8383b56998815d4c981e72c946fdbf8de77ece15e52ca2ed5c7371c8f2c8af.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to 3}{(\\frac{4f(x)-12}{{x}^{2}-2x+2})}^{2}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." :question/worked-solution "Using the power and quotient rules, we can rewrite the given limit as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}{(\\frac{4f(x)-12}{{x}^{2}-2x+2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 3}(4f(x)-12)}{{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above is true provided that  ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)$ exists.\n\nWe find from the graph that ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=4.$ We calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 3}(4f(x)-12)=4(4)-12=4\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)={3}^{2}-2(3)+2=5\n$$\n\nSo we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}{(\\frac{4f(x)-12}{{x}^{2}-2x+2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 3}(4f(x)-12)}{{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)})}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{25}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae7650e3-faf3-520c-9674-ffa036a8eacc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Power Rule to Compute a Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ded502-a64c-59eb-b7d3-1edbc975c8ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513544} {:answer/id #uuid "3ceb6ed1-d121-5435-888c-425931472192" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513691} {:answer/id #uuid "81325284-9641-5f8d-97f8-687ea6659699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513869} {:answer/id #uuid "8242f5d4-885b-5673-94ee-6897001038fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513872} {:answer/id #uuid "c0df1c26-3aa5-5e3c-8200-ef9d0a2e3adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0df1c26-3aa5-5e3c-8200-ef9d0a2e3adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514041} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f764e06-5d80-555d-8746-1b05ecbf0c86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a56b3f7-a945-5fcc-bc40-896faa412616" :question/math-academy-id "q-35282" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{z\\to (-4)}\\frac{{({z}^{2}-10)}^{2}}{(z+6)^{5}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we apply the quotient rule and the power rule to get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{z\\to (-4)}\\frac{{({z}^{2}-10)}^{2}}{(z+6)^{5}} & =\\frac{{lim}_{z\\to (-4)}{({z}^{2}-10)}^{2}}{{lim}_{z\\to (-4)}(z+6)^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{({lim}_{z\\to (-4)}({z}^{2}-10))}^{2}}{{({lim}_{z\\to (-4)}(z+6))}^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{((-4)^{2}-10)}^{2}}{(-4+6)^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}}{{2}^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1bddb74-97be-5f35-b559-afb707e6e964" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Root Rule to Compute a Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c5c60ba-65e6-5776-825d-ff0e243ef75f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513652} {:answer/id #uuid "47d1eacc-769a-58ee-9174-0153bd59ce0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513725} {:answer/id #uuid "91a02bc0-8a2d-5270-a0b4-b9c6395fc706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[7]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513910} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ba0bae-ecb1-5788-9a40-c0d5b364deaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513959} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e0271a-fd7f-5466-9403-edcedf42e03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt[7]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c5c60ba-65e6-5776-825d-ff0e243ef75f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513652} :answer-field/id #uuid "bea736b1-beb7-5da5-bed3-ff2b567324b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "813daa4e-ee7e-5bca-b4a8-b7e7146be5c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-35630" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{y\\to 128}{y}^{-1/7}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the root rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 128}{y}^{-1/7} & ={({lim}_{y\\to 128}y)}^{-1/7} \\\\  & =(128)^{-1/7} \\\\  & ={({2}^{7})}^{-1/7} \\\\  & ={2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "10100e89-21d6-53c5-a7de-f14fd73ce4b7" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Different Rules to Compute a Limit Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3e5e428-55c6-547c-8a43-b717c453f470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403267} {:answer/id #uuid "5a425311-e469-5ff8-a1bd-9454c87692d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403268} {:answer/id #uuid "deefb1bd-abfc-5373-b490-cefccc51642f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403269} {:answer/id #uuid "35d21c38-0370-5025-8bcc-f844ea185348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403270} {:answer/id #uuid "934c6624-2691-5291-bbc2-1f43189f8e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deefb1bd-abfc-5373-b490-cefccc51642f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403269} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a133e4-dd1e-5f83-ae36-ea8f3bd624c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c978569-5523-50ca-8c37-1ccfd41ba3f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-67703" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0b0074bb582011695cec9807beab1623c6aab894e0c6abeb1bf3068be6ed3543.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\frac{\\sqrt{25-f(x)}}{2}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}f(x)=9.$ \n\nApplying the root rule, we get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\frac{\\sqrt{25-f(x)}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}(25-f(x))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{25-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1bddb74-97be-5f35-b559-afb707e6e964" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Root Rule to Compute a Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "094bbce6-b3ec-5cc2-b5d6-74f6b386c8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513555} {:answer/id #uuid "36b3766c-1ae9-5be4-b0ba-9fd174da5698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513678} {:answer/id #uuid "495b98a8-0a0e-599c-827d-bc7c6e909cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513729} {:answer/id #uuid "5da93ba3-774d-5fb6-911a-3522020430fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513783} {:answer/id #uuid "b89c254c-c17d-5295-bc07-c24266eb0f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36b3766c-1ae9-5be4-b0ba-9fd174da5698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513678} :answer-field/id #uuid "32c46171-eabc-556f-8329-ffe46779d9b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "156d5c20-d8d9-52c6-bf0a-a41e2c4bb6cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-77741" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3}=\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\sqrt[3]{10x-3})}{{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-3)}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\nApplying the root rule in the numerator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}) & =\\sqrt[3]{10(3)-3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{30-3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{27} \\\\  & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the denominator, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-3) & =(3)^{2}-3 \\\\  & =6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3} & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
